<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - April 11.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - April 11.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for April 11.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Apr    211.00    215.50    216.50     224.50</p>
<p>    May    211.00    215.50    216.50     224.50</p>
<p>    Jun    206.00    210.50    211.50     221.00</p>
<p>    Jul    202.00    206.50    207.50     218.50</p>
<p>    Aug    201.00    205.50    206.50     217.50</p>
<p>    Sept   201.00    205.50    206.50     217.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$3.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	181.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  156.50	    Port Adelaide	 158.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     156.75	    Port Giles	    158.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	154.50	    Wallaroo		156.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    153.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     156.50	    Port Lincoln	  159.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   157.00	    Thevenard	     154.75</p>
<p>Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 156.00	     Esperance	    161.25</p>
<p>    Portland	157.00	     Albany		 162.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    164.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    162.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Summer Time (0530 GMT).  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
